# business-game

C++20 SFML 2D game prototype (menu + Arkanoid session). Longer-term direction is a business/board-style game; do not assume board-game features exist yet.

## Stack

- C++20, CMake ≥ 3.20, Ninja presets (`debug` / `release`)
- SFML 3.1 via FetchContent (`cmake/FetchSFML.cmake`) — no manual SFML install
- GoogleTest only in Debug; clang-format / clang-tidy at repo root

## Layout

- `src/main.cpp` — wires window, resources, event managers, screens, `GameController::run()`
- `src/controllers/` — game loop, events, scene stack
- `src/managers/` — keyboard, mouse, game-exit, game-window event managers
- `src/resources/` — `ResourceManager` (font cache)
- `src/screens/` — `MenuScreen`, `GameScreen` (`ScreenI`)
- `src/entities/` — `EntityI` implementations (`Paddle`, `Ball`, `Brick`, `Button`, …)
- `src/handlers/`, `src/window/`, `src/utils/`
- `tests/unit_tests/`, `tests/mocks/`

Static library target: `gameLib`. Executable: `game`.

## Build / test

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target game
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

Binary: `build/<preset>/bin/game` (`.exe` on Windows). Resources are copied next to the binary.

## Agent pitfalls

- Prefer interfaces (`DrawerI`, `ScreenRendererI`); avoid raw SFML in screens
- New `.cpp` files must be listed in `src/CMakeLists.txt` (`gameLib`)
- Load fonts/assets through `ResourceManager` (exe-relative paths); do not load from CWD in entities
- Screen transitions use `pushScreen` / `popScreen` / `replaceScreen` (not `setScreen`)
